  Open modal
</a>
```
      <span class="card-link hero-btn primary">Launch demo →</span>
    </a>

    <a href="/frame.json" class="component-card">
      <h3>Frame</h3>
      <p><strong>Package:</strong> inertiax-svelte</p>
      <p>Mount an Inertia page in an isolated region with its own navigation lifecycle.</p>

```svelte
<script>
  import { Frame } from 'inertiax-svelte'
</script>

<Frame id="settings-panel" src="/settings.json" />
```
      <span class="card-link hero-btn primary">Read docs →</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="info-section">
  <h3>What Inertia X adds to Inertia.js</h3>
  <div class="info-grid">
    <div class="info-item">
      <strong>&lt;Frame&gt;</strong>
      <p>Multiple independent Inertia page regions. Each frame has its own router, history, and state. Perfect for modals, sidebars, and multi-pane layouts.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="info-item">
      <strong>Global click handler</strong>
      <p>Plain <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> clicks inside a frame are auto-intercepted. No <code>&lt;Link&gt;</code> component needed.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="info-item">
      <strong>visitOptions</strong>
      <p>Set default visit behavior per frame - replace vs push, scroll preservation, URL updates.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="info-item">
      <strong>History-aware mount</strong>
      <p>Frames restore their previous page and scroll position from browser history on mount, surviving reloads.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>What Inertia X UI adds to Inertia X</h3>
  <div class="info-grid">
    <div class="info-item">
      <strong>Modal primitive</strong>
      <p><code>use:modal</code> and <code>createModal()</code> give you a fast path to modal UX built on Frame routing.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="info-item">
      <strong>Theme + structure</strong>
      <p>Ready styles like <code>dark.css</code> and <code>light.css</code>, plus predictable class hooks for easy customization.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="stack-footnote"><a href="https://inertiajs.com/">Inertia.js</a> remains the base layer: server-side routes and controllers drive your page payloads while Svelte renders the client view.</p>
</section>

<section class="info-section">
  <h2>Getting Started</h2>
  <p>Install Inertia X and Inertia X UI, then import the component API and theme.</p>

```bash
npm install inertiax-svelte inertiax-ui
```

In your app entry:

Import a theme and the components you need:

```js
import 'inertiax-ui/dark.css'
// or: import 'inertiax-ui/light.css'
import { createModal, modal } from 'inertiax-ui'
```

Use <code>use:modal</code> on links or <code>createModal()</code> to open Inertia X pages in a modal overlay.

<a href="/modal.json" class="hero-btn primary">See examples & demo →</a>
</section>

<section class="info-section">
  <h2>Styling</h2>
  <p>Inertia X UI ships with both <code>dark.css</code> and <code>light.css</code> themes. Override any CSS custom property or write your own theme from scratch.</p>
  <ul class="class-list">
    <li><code>.inx-modal_wrapper</code> - full-screen overlay</li>
    <li><code>.inx-modal_bg</code> - clickable backdrop</li>
    <li><code>.inx-modal</code> - the modal panel</li>
    <li><code>.inx-spinner</code> - loading indicator</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="hint">Svelte injects a <code>--progress</code> CSS variable (0-1) during transitions - use it for custom animations.</p>
</section>

